# CODEOWNERS — review routing and merge gating for Joshua.
#
# GitHub reads this file (not a YAML manifest) to decide who must approve a
# pull request. Every entry is `<path pattern> <owner>`; the LAST matching
# pattern wins, so keep the broad rules above the specific ones.
#
# Listed owners are auto-requested as reviewers when a PR touches their paths.
# Their approval becomes *required* to merge only once the `develop_rule`
# ruleset is enforced with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled — see the
# "Review process" section of CONTRIBUTING.md.
#
# An owner must have write access to the repository, or GitHub silently ignores
# the entry.

